                    <death when="1000-12-31"/>
                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Met Godwin during Godwin's 1800 trip to Ireland. Met at McNally's.
                            Leonard Macnally appears in the Dictionary of Irish Biography 1752-1820;
                            his uncle was a merchant called Featherstone. A Leonard Macnally married
                            Anna Maria Featherstone in 1803 or 1804. This would mean either that Mrs Featherstone
                            is an honorific title for Miss Featherstone - or that it refers to MacNally's 
                            future mother in law. </p>
